# Closed bootstrap image census checks

Run python -B tools/bootstrap-image-census-074/check.py with one fixed lane:
host, 194, 188 or metadata. No existing lane is overwritten. Linux selects nine
new private descriptor/value/provider units and the prior 21 static/model/input
regressions; none calls an original live fixture or starts a child executable.
Windows checks current-source integration and old contracts plus static build
tests. This is not new child-entry, authenticated delivery or writer-death proof.

After passing checks and committing their sources, retain.py --checked-commit SHA
verifies exact commands, log/source hashes, counts and frozen qualification, then
creates an exclusive packet. The old-prefix test inputs are models, while the
new image FD metadata/seal/access/offset checks use actual private memfds.
